{
  "requirement": "Each assessment MUST have a separate JSON usage record under\n`<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` using\n{cite}`requirements.configuration.state_location`.\nIt MUST identify its format version, run, project root, subject kind and full\nname, start time, backend and model when known, end time when finished, outcome,\naccepted determination kind (`true`, `false`, or `FIXME`) when present, and\nwhether evidence was written. It MUST record the selected output destination in\n`evidence_output` as `file` or `stdout`; a successful write to either destination\nMUST set `evidence_written` to true. Usage recording MUST remain outside the\nproject in stdout mode. FIXME entry text MUST NOT be stored in usage records.\nFailed, cancelled, or unfinished\nruns MUST remain distinguishable from completed judgments. Records MUST persist\nfor later review without storing source text, prompts, responses, or rationale.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no adequacy gap in the tests for `requirements.authoring.usage_storage`. I did not read any implementation source, because the supplied tests were enough to judge each obligation. The obligations map to tests as follows.\n\n- **Location and separate record per run.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` checks that the record is at `<state>/habeas/authoring/usage/<run_id>.json`. It checks that the file name equals `run_id`. A second `--force` run adds a second file (the directory then holds two) and leaves the first file's bytes unchanged. `fn[citation_reviews_are_confirmed_with_fresh_targeted_conversations]` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` and `fn[confirm_runs_a_second_assessment_with_its_own_usage_record]` in `tests/authoring_batch.rs` check that separate assessments get separate records. The batch tests check the record count and the outcome of each record.\n- **Identifying fields.** `fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` asserts `version`, `run_id`, the canonical `project_root`, `subject`, `subject_kind`, `backend`, `model`, `evidence_output` and `start_time_ms <= end_time_ms`. `fn[usage_subject_kind_is_known_before_sources_are_prepared]` covers the four subject kinds. `fn[usage_record_of_an_early_failure_identifies_its_subject_kind]` covers the kind for a failure before sources are prepared. `fn[authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file]` checks the recorded `model`.\n- **`evidence_output` and `evidence_written`.** `fn[stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files]` checks `evidence_output` is `stdout` and `evidence_written` is true for the true, false and FIXME determinations. `fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` checks `evidence_written` is true for the file destination. `fn[missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence]` checks `file` and `stdout` on failure with `evidence_written` false. `fn[failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage]` checks that a failed write leaves `evidence_written` false while the accepted FIXME determination is kept.\n- **Determination kind.** `fn[stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files]` covers `true`, `false` and `FIXME`. `fn[false_is_a_completed_assessment]` covers `false` in file mode. Failed runs without a determination are checked in `fn[missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence]`, where `determination` is null.\n- **Outside the project in stdout mode.** `fn[usage_state_inside_the_project_is_refused_before_creating_it]` runs both the default and `--stdout` modes with the state root inside the project. Both fail with the \"must be outside the project repository\" message, and the directory is never created.\n- **No FIXME entry text.** `fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` submits `FIXME` with `example/app#125` and asserts the serialized usage does not contain `#125`. The usage record carries only the kind string `FIXME`.\n- **Failed, cancelled and unfinished runs are distinguishable.** The unit test `fn[cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals]` in `src/authoring/usage.rs` asserts the freshly started record is `unfinished` with a null `end_time_ms`. It then asserts `cancelled` with an end time and a cancelled request. `fn[failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause]` asserts `failed` and `cancelled` outcomes with `evidence_written` false, and also covers an obstructed usage file. The CLI failure tests assert `failed`, and the success tests assert `completed`.\n- **No source text, prompts, responses or rationale.** `fn[input_metadata_counts_components_and_reads_without_persisting_source]` asserts that the serialized record omits source, requirement, term, builtin text, file names and selectors. `fn[tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text]` asserts the record omits model-chosen tool names. `fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` asserts the record omits the requirement, definition and source payload text, the rationale and the credential. `fn[authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file]` asserts the record omits the API key.\n- **State location.** `fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` runs with `XDG_STATE_HOME` pointing at a file. It also runs with `XDG_STATE_HOME` and `HOME` unset. Each run fails with non-empty stderr and empty stdout, and the previously written evidence is preserved. This applies the cited `requirements.configuration.state_location` to this subject's case.\n\nNo obligation is untested, and I found no assertion that contradicts the requirement text.",
  "references": "4b1a5eae2f231154488e098b77c5bd668b7877063fefff2bca6d98d2d5789850",
